<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CycleCare network security configuration.

  Without this file, cleartext behaviour was governed by the implicit
  targetSdk >= 28 default rather than by anything written down here,
  so the app's network posture was a side effect of a build setting
  rather than a decision.

  This app makes no plain-HTTP requests. Its only network traffic is to
  Google AdMob and Google User Messaging Platform, and both are HTTPS.

  Declared here, explicitly:
    * cleartext traffic is refused everywhere, in every build type
    * trust is anchored only in the system CA store

  Certificate pinning is deliberately NOT used. Pinning would be
  impractical against the ad and consent SDKs, which rotate
  infrastructure independently, and a wrongly pinned bundle fails closed
  for every affected user.

  When cloud sync lands (CycleCare-Redesign-Docs/17-sync-and-key-management.md),
  add a debug-only override here permitting cleartext to the emulator
  host loopback for local development. Do not widen the base config.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>